  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758869,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1 Year - Megademo (Commodore 64)\n\nPrepare to be amazed by *1 Year*, a breathtaking technical demo for the Commodore 64 that pushes the machine's capabilities to their absolute limit. Released in 1987, this isn't a game in the traditional sense, but a dazzling showcase of graphics, sound, and programming prowess. \n\nThe demo unfolds as a visual journey through a year's worth of events, presented through a series of stunning animated sequences and musical compositions. Each month is represented by a unique and often surreal scene, ranging from vibrant landscapes to abstract geometric patterns. \n\n*1 Year* is renowned for its innovative use of parallax scrolling, detailed sprite animation, and a memorable, synthesized soundtrack. It’s a testament to the creativity and skill of the demo scene, offering a glimpse into the cutting-edge possibilities of the Commodore 64. While there's no traditional gameplay, the sheer spectacle and technical achievement make *1 Year* a must-see for any retro computing enthusiast. Experience the peak of 8-bit artistry!"
    },
